WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.440
Claude. Codex. Cursor.

2
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:06.680
Antigravity. Four brilliant AI coders, in four different apps.

3
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.270
And you're the one copying messages between them.

4
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:13.200
Crewroom puts them in one room, as one team,

5
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:14.510
on your own computer.

6
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.370
Pick a folder and hire your crew.

7
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.010
Every member gets an agent, a model, and the

8
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.240
roles it plays.

9
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.580
Cursor and Antigravity now sit beside Claude and Codex.

10
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.380
Crewroom checks that each one is installed, and a

11
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.810
step-by-step guide gets them signed in.

12
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.900
Hand out a plant care page, and they pass

13
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:37.020
the work along.

14
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.540
Research, icons, code, and a review that sends fixes

15
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.130
back.

16
00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.540
Not sure what to build next?

17
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.300
Write at team in Discussion.

18
00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.940
They talk it through in turns, answer each other

19
00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.450
by name, and the host writes the decision.

20
00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:01.290
Tag anyone mid-job to change course.

21
00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:02.600
Or just say stop.

22
00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.760
Crewroom installs and updates like a real app on

23
00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.600
Windows, runs on macOS and Linux too, and always

24
00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.990
shows you when it's running.

25
00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:14.910
Stop being the messenger.

26
00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:16.300
Start leading the team.

27
00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:20.840
Crewroom. Free and open source.
